.Dd July 10, 2026
.Dt LIBBLEMESH 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libblemesh
.Nd Bluetooth BLE-mesh protocol library
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libblemesh
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mesh_crypto.h
.In mesh_net.h
.In mesh_transport.h
.In mesh_access.h
.In mesh_cfg_model.h
.In mesh_health_model.h
.In mesh_generic.h
.In mesh_sensor.h
.In mesh_time_scene.h
.In mesh_provision.h
.In mesh_beacon.h
.In mesh_iv.h
.In mesh_rpl.h
.In mesh_key_refresh.h
.In mesh_proxy.h
.In mesh_friend.h
.In mesh_relay.h
.In mesh_sim.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library implements the Bluetooth Mesh Protocol
.Pq Vt MshPRT_v1.1
and Bluetooth Mesh Model
.Pq Vt MshMDL_v1.1
specifications as a set of pure, hardware-free modules.
Every codec and security function performs no I/O, keeps no global state,
and returns
.Va 0
on success or
.Va -1
on failure with its output zeroed; secrets are cleared with
.Xr explicit_bzero 3 .
The stack layers, bottom to top, are:
.Bl -tag -width "mesh_health_model" -offset indent
.It Fn mesh_crypto
Salt/key-derivation
.Pq Vt s1 , Vt k1 , Vt k2 , Vt k3 , Vt k4 ,
network/application nonces and the AES-CCM primitives.
.It Fn mesh_net
Network-layer obfuscation, encryption and NID matching.
.It Fn mesh_transport
Lower/upper transport, SAR segmentation and reassembly.
.It Fn mesh_access
The cleartext opcode/parameter codec and the model-dispatch registry.
.It Fn mesh_cfg_model , Fn mesh_health_model
The mandatory Configuration and Health foundation models.
.It Fn mesh_generic
The Generic OnOff, Generic Level, Generic Default Transition Time, Generic
Power OnOff, and Generic Power Level application models, including their
required state bindings and setup-server procedures.
.It Fn mesh_sensor
The Sensor Server, Sensor Setup Server, and Sensor Client models, including
Descriptor, Sensor, Column, Series, Cadence, Settings, and Setting procedures.
.It Fn mesh_time_scene
The Time, Scene, and Scheduler Server, Setup Server, and Client models,
including Mesh Time encodings, Scene snapshot callbacks, and Scheduler
register codecs.
.It Fn mesh_provision
The provisioning protocol: PDU codec, ECDH P-256, the security functions and
the PB-ADV / PB-GATT bearers.
.It Fn mesh_beacon , Fn mesh_iv , Fn mesh_key_refresh
The Secure Network beacon and the IV-Update and Key-Refresh state machines.
.It Fn mesh_rpl , Fn mesh_relay , Fn mesh_proxy , Fn mesh_friend
Replay protection and the Relay, Proxy and Friend features.
.El
.Pp
The
.In mesh_sim.h
module wires the layers into an in-process, multi-node mesh network over a
shared virtual advertising medium: it is the spec-oracle harness that drives
the full receive pipeline
.Pq deobfuscate, decrypt, cache, relay, reassemble, dispatch
without any radio hardware.
.Ss Node lifecycle
A typical embedding provisions a node, installs its keys, registers its
models and pumps received Access PDUs through the access-layer dispatcher:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct mesh_sim sim;
struct mesh_node *node;
struct mesh_gen_onoff_srv onoff;

mesh_sim_init(&sim, netkey, appkey, iv_index);
node = mesh_sim_add_node(&sim, 0x0001, 1);

mesh_gen_onoff_srv_init(&onoff, MESH_GEN_OFF);
mesh_sim_add_model(node, 0, mesh_gen_onoff_srv_model(&onoff));

/* Originate, then run the medium to quiescence. */
mesh_sim_send_access(&sim, node, 0xFFFF,
    MESH_OP_GEN_ONOFF_STATUS, params, plen, 0x04);
mesh_sim_run(&sim, 16);
.Ed
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
Multi-octet fields are big-endian on the network layer and little-endian at
the access layer, matching the specifications.
The
.Nm
provisioning and crypto modules link against
.Xr crypto 3
for ECDH P-256 and the AES primitives.
When the kernel is built
.Cm WITH_DTRACE
the library also publishes the
.Va mesh
USDT provider
.Pq 34 probes across the network, transport, access, replay, IV, key-refresh,
beacon, friend, provisioning and proxy layers .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crypto 3 ,
.Xr libble 3 ,
.Xr meshd 8
